       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg for adults. A single 1,600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and there is no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for adults, usually reserved for inflammatory conditions.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day). This is a common dose for pain or fever.\n\nPerhaps you meant 1,600 mg per day in total, or 400 mg four times daily. Tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. I can also add a note, such as \"give with food.\""
